 both the same slope $\\frac{3}{4}$ and the same $y$-intercept $5$ as the given line. It is the same line, so it is not a distinct parallel line.\n\nThe line $3x-4y=-4$ has slope $\\frac{3}{4}$ and $y$-intercept $1$, different from $5$. Therefore, it is a distinct parallel line.\n\n$$\n3x-4y=-4\n$$" 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721201 1075 #edb/ref 17592186721208 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721201 1075 #edb/ref 17592186721209 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721201 1075 #edb/ref 17592186721214 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721201 1075 #edb/ref 17592186721217 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721201 1075 #edb/ref 17592186721220 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721201 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721201 1077 "selection" 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721201 1078 #edb/ref 17592186721208 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721201 1079 #uuid "066af54e-4514-5447-9fd7-c69d34adacad" 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721202 1080 "-12x-2y=8" 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721202 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721202 1083 #uuid "0a0ca3f8-6ec2-5ceb-9420-61226acb9dbd" 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721203 1068 #edb/ref 17592186721216 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721203 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721203 1071 "Which of the following is a distinct line parallel to $10x+2y=4$?" 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721203 1072 #uuid "29a84886-3c12-5e30-b049-a6317548bbd1" 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721203 1074 "For two distinct nonvertical lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\nTo find the slope of $10x+2y=4$, convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n10x+2y &= 4 \\\\\n2y &= -10x+4 \\\\\ny &= -5x+2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe slope is the coefficient of $x$, so the required slope is $-5$.\n\nRewrite the choices in slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-10x-2y=10 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-5x-5 \\\\\n3x-3y=12 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=x-4 \\\\\n-4x-3y=9 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-\\frac{4}{3}x-3 \\\\\n2x-2y=-10 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=x+5 \\\\\n5x+y=2 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-5x+2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe line $5x+y=2$ has both the same slope $-5$ and the same $y$-intercept $2$ as the given line. It is the same line, so it is not a distinct parallel line.\n\nThe line $-10x-2y=10$ has slope $-5$ and $y$-intercept $-5$, different from $2$. Therefore, it is a distinct parallel line.\n\n$$\n-10x-2y=10\n$$" 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721204 1080 "-6x-3y=3" 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721204 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721204 1083 #uuid "36a83a6f-2d62-57f9-8425-cb0c80fa082f" 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721205 1080 "-10x-2y=10" 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721205 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721205 1083 #uuid "3bd93cf0-58ea-56ef-a91e-38fee93c71ce" 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721206 1080 "8x-2y=4" 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721206 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721206 1083 #uuid "42aca68b-60af-54c1-854c-23e6ca28379b" 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721207 1080 "9x+12y=-36" 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721207 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721207 1083 #uuid "43a6ff67-f7b6-5ba9-bde9-fdf764e26855" 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721208 1080 "-6x-9y=0" 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721208 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721208 1083 #uuid "4d72d442-1b42-551e-bbdc-94f8e6f505c6" 13194139541870 1759