true] [17592186721227 1068 #edb/ref 17592186721201 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721227 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721227 1071 "Which of the following is a distinct line parallel to $2x+3y=-15$?" 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721227 1072 #uuid "ccc0b544-1bb9-5c7b-86fb-fc4b22388c64" 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721227 1074 "For two distinct nonvertical lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\nTo find the slope of $2x+3y=-15$, convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x+3y &= -15 \\\\\n3y &= -2x-15 \\\\\ny &= -\\frac{2}{3}x-5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe slope is the coefficient of $x$, so the required slope is $-\\frac{2}{3}$.\n\nRewrite the choices in slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x+6y=-30 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-\\frac{2}{3}x-5 \\\\\n-4x+6y=-24 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=\\frac{2}{3}x-4 \\\\\n-3x-6y=12 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-\\frac{1}{2}x-2 \\\\\n-4x+6y=24 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=\\frac{2}{3}x+4 \\\\\n-6x-9y=0 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-\\frac{2}{3}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe line $4x+6y=-30$ has both the same slope $-\\frac{2}{3}$ and the same $y$-intercept $-5$ as the given line. It is the same line, so it is not a distinct parallel line.\n\nThe line $-6x-9y=0$ has slope $-\\frac{2}{3}$ and $y$-intercept $0$, different from $-5$. Therefore, it is a distinct parallel line.\n\n$$\n-6x-9y=0\n$$" 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721228 1080 "6x+2y=8" 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721228 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721228 1083 #uuid "d1c6e703-9466-5a38-8478-8ca4ed630792" 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721229 1075 #edb/ref 17592186721206 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721229 1075 #edb/ref 17592186721222 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721229 1075 #edb/ref 17592186721228 1319413954