 parallel line.\n\nThe line $8x-2y=4$ has slope $4$ and $y$-intercept $-2$, different from $3$. Therefore, it is a distinct parallel line.\n\n$$\n8x-2y=4\n$$" 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721232 1080 "-18x-3y=-6" 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721232 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721232 1083 #uuid "ee1576d8-f766-5770-b29f-8346e71406fd" 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721233 1068 #edb/ref 17592186721224 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721233 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721233 1071 "Which of the following is a distinct line parallel to $18x+3y=-12$?" 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721233 1072 #uuid "f8d1fb4f-c4dd-590a-ab1d-79c15fd0ec08" 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721233 1074 "For two distinct nonvertical lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\nTo find the slope of $18x+3y=-12$, convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n18x+3y &= -12 \\\\\n3y &= -18x-12 \\\\\ny &= -6x-4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe slope is the coefficient of $x$, so the required slope is $-6$.\n\nRewrite the choices in slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-12x-2y=8 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-6x-4 \\\\\n9x+12y=-24 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-\\frac{3}{4}x-2 \\\\\n-18x-3y=-6 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-6x+2 \\\\\n9x+12y=-36 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-\\frac{3}{4}x-3 \\\\\n-6x+8y=-24 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=\\frac{3}{4}x-3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe line $-12x-2y=8$ has both the same slope $-6$ and the same $y$-intercept $-4$ as the given line. It is the same line, so it is not a distinct parallel line.\n\nThe line $-18x-3y=-6$ has slope $-6$ and $y$-intercept $2$, different from $-4$. Therefore, it is a distinct parallel line.\n\n$$\n-18x-3y=-6\n$$" 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592186721234 1080 "-12x-9y=18" 13194139541870 17592186045443 true] [17592